---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageNav from '../../components/PageNav.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Overview">
    <div class="page-header">
        <h1>Evidence-Driven Delivery</h1>
        <p class="page-header-desc">
            A structural model for managing uncertainty, governing build progression,
            and determining when work becomes commitment.
        </p>
        <div class="page-meta">
            <span class="page-reading-time">2 min read</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="hero-section">
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-secondary);max-width:640px;">
            Traditional delivery models advance work by time. Phases complete on schedule,
            handoffs occur at predetermined milestones, and commitment scales with calendar
            position — not with validated understanding.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-secondary);max-width:640px;margin-top:16px;">
            Evidence-Driven Delivery inverts this. Work advances by <strong style="color:var(--text);font-weight:500;">confidence</strong>.
            Investment scales only when uncertainty has been measurably reduced. Commitment
            is governed by evidence, not elapsed time.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>What This Specification Covers</h2>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
            <a href="/philosophy/" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border);text-decoration:none;color:inherit;" class="edd-link">
                <div>
                    <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:4px;">Philosophy</div>
                    <div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);">The Shift</div>
                    <div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:2px;line-height:1.5;">From time-boxed discovery to continuous uncertainty reduction through confidence gates.</div>
                </div>
                <span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-tertiary);flex-shrink:0;padding-left:24px;">→</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/model/operating-model/" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border);text-decoration:none;color:inherit;" class="edd-link">
                <div>
                    <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:4px;">The Model</div>
                    <div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);">Operating Model</div>
                    <div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:2px;line-height:1.5;">Multi-dimensional model: Evidence Work, Build Lifecycle, and SDLC as independent dimensions.</div>
                </div>
                <span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-tertiary);flex-shrink:0;padding-left:24px;">→</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/practice/backlogs/" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border);text-decoration:none;color:inherit;" class="edd-link">
                <div>
                    <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:4px;">In Practice</div>
                    <div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);">Dual Backlogs &amp; Engagement</div>
                    <div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:2px;line-height:1.5;">Evidence and Commitment backlogs, 8-week engagement shape, and traced risk examples.</div>
                </div>
                <span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-tertiary);flex-shrink:0;padding-left:24px;">→</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/reference/" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-decoration:none;color:inherit;" class="edd-link">
                <div>
                    <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:4px;">Reference</div>
                    <div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);">Glossary &amp; Constraints</div>
                    <div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:2px;line-height:1.5;">Operating model terms, operational constraints, and what this model does and does not define.</div>
                </div>
                <span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-tertiary);flex-shrink:0;padding-left:24px;">→</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>About This Document</h2>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-muted);">
            This is an internal operating specification for Sparq. It defines the structural model for how we manage uncertainty,
            govern build progression, and determine when work becomes commitment.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-tertiary);margin-top:12px;font-family:var(--mono);">v1.0 — Initial specification (February 2026)</p>
    </section>

    <PageNav next={{ href: "/philosophy/", title: "The Shift" }} />
</BaseLayout>
